# Component Rules

## File Structure
- One component per file. File name matches component name in PascalCase.
- Co-locate component, styles, tests, and types in the same directory.
- Barrel export via `index.ts` at the component directory level.

## Props
- Define props interfaces with the component name prefix: `{ComponentName}Props`.
- Destructure props in the function signature.
- Use explicit types -- no `any`.
- Document non-obvious props with JSDoc comments.
- Provide default values where sensible.

## Component Design
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Keep components under 150 lines. Extract sub-components or hooks for longer ones.
- Separate container (data/logic) from presentational (rendering) components.
- Use hooks/composables for reusable stateful logic.

## Naming
- Components: PascalCase (`UserCard`, `SearchInput`).
- Event handler props: prefix with `on` (`onClick`, `onSubmit`).
- Event handler implementations: prefix with `handle` (`handleClick`, `handleSubmit`).
- Boolean props: prefix with `is`, `has`, `should` (`isDisabled`, `hasError`).

## Styling
- Use the project's established styling approach ({STYLING_APPROACH}).
- Avoid inline styles except for truly dynamic values.
- Use design tokens / CSS variables for colors, spacing, typography.
- Responsive: mobile-first, use defined breakpoints.

## Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements (`button` not `div` with onClick).
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Provide `aria-label` for icon-only buttons.
- Ensure sufficient color contrast ratios.
- Inputs must have associated labels.

## Performance
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders. Profile before memoizing.
- Lazy-load components that are not above-the-fold.
- Virtualize long lists (>100 items).
- Avoid expensive computation in render. Move to hooks or memoize.

## Testing
- Test user-visible behavior, not implementation details.
- Use testing-library queries that reflect how users interact (getByRole, getByText).
- Cover: default render, user interactions, error states, loading states.
- Mock external dependencies, not sibling components.
